                    "line": 236,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Naresh Solanki",
                        "email": "naresh.solanki@9elements.com",
                        "username": "nsolanki22"
                    },
                    "message": "What duration do you recommend ?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/views/HardwareStatus/Sensors/Sensors.vue",
                    "line": 236,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Gunnar Mills",
                        "email": "gunnar@gmills.xyz",
                        "username": "gtmills"
                    },
                    "message": "Let's look at MetricReportDefinition.. Or getting something like $expand in"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/views/HardwareStatus/Sensors/Sensors.vue",
                    "line": 236,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jason Westover",
                        "email": "jwestover@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "j-westover"
                    },
                    "message": "When a polling solution ever comes up it should always invite scrutiny. \nI would look at your requirements and determine what you are trying to solve.\nIf it is about stale data, that is what the WebUI refresh button is for (actually a feature that should eventually go away once we have sufficient UI updates via SSE).\nIf you need something more than a refresh button, I would look into Ed's suggestion of looking at MetricReportDefinition for streaming or possibly something else like a collection that could take advantage of ETags.  Calling hundreds of Sensors over and over again should never be the answer."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/views/HardwareStatus/Sensors/Sensors.vue",
                    "line": 236,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Nikhil Ashoka",
                        "email": "a.nikhil@ibm.com",
                        "username": "Nikhil-Ashoka"
                    },
                    "message": "For this: \n\"Our downstream version, for example, has ~24 Chassis objects that have Sensors collections. Fetching all ~250 total Sensors takes ~60.7 seconds\"\n\nAs Gunnar suggested \"getting something like $expand in\" will help improve the time\n\nReference:\nhttps://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/webui-vue/+/71290"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/views/HardwareStatus/Sensors/Sensors.vue",
                    "line": 236,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jason Westover",
                        "email": "jwestover@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "j-westover"
                    },
                    "message": "Yes! Ed's quick example: `curl -u root:password -k https://bmc/redfish/v1/Chassis\\?\\$expand\\=.\\(\\$levels\\=3\\) | jq '.Members[] | .Sensors | .Members[]? | {\"reading\": .Reading, \"name\": .Name}'` Reduces that time to 27 seconds!  You would still not want to poll that however!\n\nI am really looking forward to incorporating odata queries into the project.  We would have to have a generalized query API (something as simple as `api.query()`) that would handle supported queries (i.e. check the Expand/MaxLevels) and fallback to redpath when they are not supported (or tagged as too slow - it's possible for expand to be slower on some systems for example)."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/views/HardwareStatus/Sensors/Sensors.vue",
                    "line": 236,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Naresh Solanki",
                        "email": "naresh.solanki@9elements.com",
                        "username": "nsolanki22"
                    },
                    "message": "Acknowledged"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/views/HardwareStatus/Sensors/Sensors.vue",
                    "line": 236,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "> What duration do you recommend ?\n\n\nI would not recommend a duration.  Stream the values from MetricReport."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/views/HardwareStatus/Sensors/Sensors.vue",
                    "line": 236,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jason Westover",
                        "email": "jwestover@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "j-westover"
                    },
                    "message": "> Stream the values from MetricReport.\n\nThat would be really cool to see!  \ud83d\udc4d"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/views/HardwareStatus/Sensors/Sensors.vue",
                    "line": 236,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Naresh Solanki",
                        "email": "naresh.solanki@9elements.com",
                        "username": "nsolanki22"
                    },
                    "message": "I'm kind of stuck here.\nI've created Metric report But I do nnot get update in SSE\nI've checked enable & seems fine to me.\nI would need some expert input to proceed further."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/views/HardwareStatus/Sensors/Sensors.vue",
                    "line": 236,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Naresh Solanki",
                        "email": "naresh.solanki@9elements.com",
                        "username": "nsolanki22"
                    },
                    "message": "@ed@tanous.net @jwestover@nvidia.com\n\nI've got MetricReport + SSE thing working(using curl command) & below are my findings:\n\n  There is limit to number of MetricReportDefinitions\nIf multiples sensors are added withing a single MetricReportDefinition, then all the sensor data is sent even if there is change in one sensor data(if onChange is used)\n\nIf MetricReport/SSE with Periodic reporting is used then the current patchset seems much better & simple because the SSE Even handler only gets value + odata.id  so basically this needs to be mapped to sensor name.\n\nThis understanding I've arrived based on my observations & testing.\nI don't see much advantage here unless I missed something(feel free to correct me)"
                }
            ],
